# Supabase connection.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in from your project's
# Settings → API page. Leave both blank (or delete the file) and the app runs
# entirely on local data exactly as before — no network, no backend.
#
# The anon key is safe in the browser: it is public by design, and row-level
# security in supabase/schema.sql is what actually protects the data.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional. Used only by the scheduled keep-warm ping in api/keep-warm.js, which
# stops Supabase pausing a Free-plan project after a week of no activity.
#
# The function falls back to the two variables above, so on Vercel there is
# nothing extra to set. CRON_SECRET is Vercel's own: set it on the project and
# Vercel sends it as a bearer token, which stops anyone else calling the
# endpoint. Neither belongs in the browser bundle, so neither is VITE_-prefixed.

# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# CRON_SECRET=
